  "v3": "Adds the penicillin-class and sulfonamide-antibiotic members of data/rules/allergy.json (brands and generics) so an allergy check can be reached from a typed or photographed label. Names only for combination partners (clavulanate, sulbactam, tazobactam): no rule covers them.",
  "v2": "Adds every drug named in the router's bucket universe (B, data/buckets/v5) plus codeine and St. John's wort, so a typed or photographed name reaches the router. Multi-word ingredient ids use underscores (st_johns_wort). Salt forms collapse to the universe's id: isosorbide mononitrate/dinitrate -> isosorbide; valproic acid/divalproex -> valproate. Names only: no new rules, so no new flags (I4).",
  "source": "Authored for the demo from US brand/generic names (FDA Orange Book / DailyMed listings). Synthetic project; not a complete formulary.",
  "note": "Keys are lowercase names as written on labels or typed. Values are generic ingredients, in the order a combination label lists its strengths (e.g. Zestoretic 10/12.5 = lisinopril 10, hydrochlorothiazide 12.5). Every ingredient is also recognized under its own name.",
